Subject: [PATCH] Babel: add route hysteresis and independent ETX loss weight

Keep a usable selected route until a feasible alternative has been better
by the configured margin for 30 seconds. Reevaluate using the existing
Babel timer, even when subsequent Updates carry the same metric. A route
that becomes unusable still fails over immediately.

On wireless interfaces, retain the existing 16-Hello loss estimator and
apply a floor to its ETX excess weight. Lossless costs and reachability
checks are unchanged. This keeps loss significant even with a low base
metric.

Optional directives in the Babel protocol block:
  etx loss scale 128;    # minimum loss weight, 0..65534
  hysteresis margin 24;  # required improvement, 0..65534

These defaults apply when the directives are omitted. A zero loss scale
uses the original ETX weight. A zero margin still requires a strictly
better metric and the 30-second hold. Photon can set the lossless base
to 32 on both peers via routing.instances[].metric_base.

Applies to BIRD 2.19.3 with patch -p1.

